cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QECCertificates in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "QECCertificates: checkable distance certificates for quantum error correction"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 library for certified quantum error correction: the GF(2) and symplectic
  machinery that turns a code parameter into a checkable statement, an in-kernel checker
  for LRAT certificates together with its soundness theorem, and encoding faithfulness in
  both directions, so that a model of the encoded CNF is a light logical operator. Alongside
  them it carries the layers in which a fault-tolerance statement is read: the cochain
  complexes of a circuit with their mapping cones and Kunneth formulas, spacetime fault
  distance, the cosystolic distance, the auxiliary hypergraph and the subcode layer, and the
  abstract closure theorem for syndrome-exhaustive check matrices. Every load-bearing
  declaration is printed in an audit region and depends on no axioms beyond the three
  standard ones.
type: software
